 R←Test_25(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;⎕IO;⎕ML;trap;list;fno;crash;own;QEN
⍝ `crash` reports the caller's ⎕IO, ⎕ML and ⎕TRAP, and the stack holds none of HandleError's own functions
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

⍝ Preconditions...
 #.⎕SHADOW'HandleErrorParms'
 #.HandleErrorParms←##.HandleError.CreateParms
 #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder←GetTempPath⊃⎕SI
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDir #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder
 {}'CREATE!'FilesAndDirs.CheckPath #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder
 trap←(405 'E' '406 ##.HandleError.Process #.HandleErrorParms')(406 'C' '→∆CarryOn')(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')

⍝ No :Trap around the error here: within a :Trap, ⎕TRAP reports that :Trap (`406 ':'`) instead of the real setting
 ⎕TRAP←trap
 trap←⎕TRAP                                       ⍝ The form Dyalog reports it in
 ⎕IO←0 ⋄ ⎕ML←3
 {⎕SIGNAL ⍵}405
 ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1

∆CarryOn:
 QEN←⎕EN
 ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')

 →T.GoToTidyUp 406≠QEN
 list←FilesAndDirs.ListFiles #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder,'/*.dcf'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≠≢list
 fno←(⊃list)⎕FTIE 0
 crash←⎕FREAD fno 1
 ⎕FUNTIE fno
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≢crash.IO
 →T.GoToTidyUp 3≢crash.ML
 →T.GoToTidyUp trap≢crash.Trap
 own←(⍕##.HandleError),'.'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0=≢crash.XSI
 →T.GoToTidyUp∨/(⊂own)≡¨(≢own)↑¨crash.XSI
 →T.GoToTidyUp(≢crash.XSI)≢≢crash.LC

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDir #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder
